    "text": "live5news.com\nwebsite\nNorth Charleston\nMan expected to face charges after leading North Charleston Police on chase\nBy Patrick Phillips,\n15 hours agoNORTH CHARLESTON, S.C. (WCSC) - North Charleston Police say a man wanted on one charge is likely to face at least one additional charge following a Monday night chase. Kelvin McArthur Johnson, 56, is charged with one count of second-degree burglary, according to Charleston County jail records. A North Charleston Police incident report states officers expected to file a charge of failure to stop for blue lights and siren.\n6",
